  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14231437/assets/a1f53be1baf6a5db5807565f0511813cb41a7b48ec42e37a96049403aaa2235d.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}$ between $x=0$, $x=5$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $k.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4}$\n{{field-1}}",
